00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:03.909 align:start position:0%
 
mr vice president  i look out over my biden sign in my  front yard  and i see a sea of drum flags and yard  signs  that's a voter at a joe biden town hall  in pennsylvania last month  raising the topic of lawn signs the  cardboard rectangles may not be a  scientific gauge necessarily of  political support  but they are impossible to ignore giving  both supporters of a candidate and  campaign operatives a sense of optimism  or concern  and as brook silva braga found out the  sign wars have taken a new turn this  year  [Music]  it's hard to say if they prove anything  about the direction of an election  [Music]  [Applause]  just the same as like putting out the  american flag you know showing what side  what side you're on but these october  ornaments  for our divided times i love to decorate  anyway  maybe the simplest most public way to  make a political stand  and i said you know we had a smaller  sign in 2016. it's 2020 we have a big  sign  political yard signs have long dotted  the american landscape  but four years ago something seemed  different  how long have you been into the signs  probably since the 2016 election  a certain anti-establishment campaign  found fertile ground in american lawns  what was the motivation the candidate  the candidate in his story  from jeannie chase's new hampshire yard  to gloria gibert's pennsylvania spread  trump signs bloomed something about  candidate trump  made you want to be public about your  support in a way you hadn't been for  other candidates  a lot of people were getting disgusted  with politicians in general they say one  thing and do another thing  i'm getting goosebumps because this man  i'm telling you we just have a lot of  faith in  him but the carpet of signs from the  master marketer  did not sit well with mark graziadio the  other party gave him out like  like candy he's the democratic chairman  for wayne county in rural northeast  pennsylvania  yes it's a republican stronghold but  grazia dio knew there was another reason  his party got  trounced in the 2016 sign war  even in states like pennsylvania where  trump won the vote by  less than one percent we were unable to  get signs and people wait what does that  mean  unable to get signs the campaign just  wouldn't provide them for us  they thought the signs were a waste of  time um they didn't think that they were  effective  but see where we think they're effective  is not so much in getting people to  change their minds  but to reinforce that there are other  people here who think like you do  if you only see signs for the other  candidate then you may think you're  overwhelmed  jeff eggleston another pennsylvania  democrat  certainly felt overwhelmed last election  night huge news  actually the ap now projecting that  donald trump has won the state of  pennsylvania  i went to bed and my wife you know cried  you know i mean we were  we were devastated and i realized at  that time that i hadn't  done enough so in 2020 rolled around  eggleston whose long-supported  democratic campaigns  decided the contribution he could make  was designing  and printing his own joe biden signs  they did one delivery  around the state how many signs uh 12  000. okay that's a lot of signs that was  a lot you know i was  i was doing cartwheels down the street i  was telling everybody i delivered 12 000  signs you know  before you knew it all these people saw  him and said hey i want those signs  and so then we did an order for 30 000.  then we did an order for 40 000 and then  we did another order for 20 000. who's  we  um well me and that was how jeff  eggleston  came to drive 4 000 miles across  pennsylvania  and delivered nearly 150 000 joe biden  signs  defying his party's conventional wisdom  from my  experience it started with the obama  campaign and it became like a dogma  within the campaign  community that you just don't deal with  it at all  why the democratic party can be very  cerebral  we've done studies that show if you call  somebody this percentage of the time you  can sway them  when someone puts a yard sign in the  yard it's really hard for us to quantify  what the effect is  that that has on people so do they prove  anything about the direction of an  election  columbia university professor donald  green is one of the few  to seriously research the answer we  found an average effect of about a  1.7 percentage point boost so  a candidate who would ordinarily get  48.3 would get 50.0  in a close race that could make the  difference  but the research tracked small local  elections  green hasn't studied the impact on  presidential races  because of a legal obstacle we have a  bit of a difficulty where we can't use  university funds to buy lawn signs you  would need someone to donate the signs  that's right getting to the bottom of  this is something we certainly can do  for now the best evidence of at least  their psychological impact  may be how opponents treat them  vandalism has become a bipartisan vice  which only makes the wagner floyd  household  that much more remarkable all our  neighbors think we're crazy  yeah they don't understand it joe wagner  and megan floyd are lifelong best  friends  and co-owners of this house in johnstown  pennsylvania  with a conspicuously divided front yard  so where are we now with the signs we  got three each right three  been matching each other sign for sign  for months  and yet somehow have not let the names  on the cardboard  come between them i actually fixed the  one too because yeah  it didn't fix my one bottom side inside  and what does that feel like isn't that  just totally going against what you're  trying to do  i felt like such a traitor i'm just  kidding  you know she has her her views and i  have my views and  we can try to agree to disagree  lawn signs do not tell us who will win  tuesday  but they do prove something important  about the election  i'm just pushing for a brighter future  as the sign says  support for the political process itself  that's their choice just like i'm having  my choice  for cbs this morning saturday brook  silva braga in wayne county pennsylvania  i love that couple i love everything  about that couple the fact that they can  still get along and yet have such  disparate points of view but here's the  bottom line with with lawn science you  leave nothing on the table in a campaign  and if you have the money you know you  need to spend the money and i think that  a few elections ago you know folks  thought the money should go elsewhere  it's a reminder it just stands out in  your mind i don't  impact it has but it's there yeah it's  still nice that joe helped megan  it is

